# @@APP@@

Targets Platform Architecture Guide @@GUIDE_VERSION@@.

@@APP_DESCRIPTION@@

`@@APP@@` is a **@@APP_KIND@@ app** of the platform (guide chapter 11).
@@IF IS_CORE@@
It owns the portal (the Vue shell every app plugs into), the backend and
frontend sdks other apps import, and the platform services.
@@ENDIF IS_CORE@@
@@IFNOT IS_CORE@@
It requires `@@CORE_APP@@` (the core app) and imports from it only
`@@CORE_APP@@.sdk` (backend) and the portal sdk and shared code (frontend).
@@ENDIF IS_CORE@@
@@IF IS_FOUNDATION@@
It holds business primitives shared by feature apps; other apps use it through
`@@APP@@.public`. It has no portal frontend.
@@ENDIF IS_FOUNDATION@@

| Path | Holds |
|---|---|
| `@@APP@@/hooks.py` | Frappe wiring only (BE-STR-003) |
| `@@APP@@/modules.txt` | One Frappe module per feature, plus `@@APP_MODULE@@ Shared` (BE-STR-001) |
| `@@APP@@/@@APP@@_shared/` | Code shared by two or more features (BE-STR-004) |
@@IF IS_CORE@@
| `@@APP@@/sdk/` | The backend sdk: the only part of this app other apps import (BE-SDK-001) |
| `@@APP@@/www/portal.py` | The portal page controller; `portal.html` is written by the frontend build |
| `frontend/` | The portal: shell, core features, sdk, shared code, styles, and the toolchain that builds, lints and tests every app's frontend (guide 10) |
@@ENDIF IS_CORE@@
@@IFNOT IS_CORE@@
| `@@APP@@/public/` | The public backend surface other apps may import (BE-INT-001) |
@@ENDIF IS_CORE@@
@@IF IS_FEATURE@@
| `frontend/` | The app's portal frontend: `manifest.ts`, one slice per feature under `features/`; built, linted and tested by the core app's toolchain (FE-COMP-006) |
@@ENDIF IS_FEATURE@@
| `docs/` | `conformance.md` and the ADRs of this repository |

## Working on it

The checkout lives in `frappe-bench/apps/@@APP@@` of the development
environment. Recipes run in the development container (ADR 0002):

```bash
just                       # list the recipes
just setup                 # platform checkout, dependencies, hook environments
just ci                    # what CI runs on every pull request
just test-backend          # Frappe tests on the minimal test site
```
@@IF IS_CORE@@

The portal is served at `/portal` of the development site once built
(`just build`); `just dev` starts the Vite dev server with hot reload.
@@ENDIF IS_CORE@@

Shared tool configuration (`ruff.toml`, `mypy.ini`, `.pre-commit-config.yaml`,
…) comes from the platform repository at the commit pinned in the `justfile`:
change it there, then `just sync-config` (DEL-TOOL-003).

## Conformance

This repository targets the guide; the rules that do not hold yet are listed in
[`docs/conformance.md`](docs/conformance.md). It switches to "Conforms to" when
that list is empty and CI passes (FND-CONF-006). Until then it is not added to
`platform.lock` (FND-CONF-005).

